{title: O Come, All Ye Faithful}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}

[G]O come, all ye [D]faithful, [G]joyful [D7]and tri[G]um[D]phant,
[Em]O come [A]ye, O [D]come [G]ye to [D]Beth[A7]le[D]hem;
[G]Come [Am]and be[D7]hold [G]Him, [D]born the [Em]King of [D]angels;

{label: Chorus}
[G]O come, let [D7]us a[G]dore Him,
O come, let [D7]us a[G]dore [D]Him,
O [Am]come, let [A7]us a[D]dore [C]Him,
[G]Christ [D]the [G]Lord.

Sing, choirs of angels, sing in exultation,
Sing, all ye citizens of heaven above;
Glory to God, glory in the highest;

{label: Chorus}
[G]O come, let [D7]us a[G]dore Him,
O come, let [D7]us a[G]dore [D]Him,
O [Am]come, let [A7]us a[D]dore [C]Him,
[G]Christ [D]the [G]Lord.

Yea, Lord, we greet Thee, born this happy morning,
Jesus, to Thee be glory given;
Word of the Father, now in flesh appearing;

{label: Chorus}
[G]O come, let [D7]us a[G]dore Him,
O come, let [D7]us a[G]dore [D]Him,
O [Am]come, let [A7]us a[D]dore [C]Him,
[G]Christ [D]the [G]Lord.
